==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* [[myocardial infarct]]

===Etymology===
From  greek [[ἔμφραγμα]] (obstacle) [[του]] (οφ) [[μυοκάρδιο|μυοκαρδίου]] (heart muscle)

===Noun===
{{en-noun|sg=[[myocardial]] [[infarction]]}}

# {{cardiology|pathology}} [[necrosis|Necrosis]] of heart muscle caused by an interruption to the supply of [[blood]] to the [[heart]], often as a result of [[coronary thrombosis]].

====Synonyms====
* [[cardiac infarction]]
* [[heart attack]]

====See also====
* [[angina pectoris]]
* [[heart failure]]

